From 52b9561774d7bf8ee49835385640e217602a412d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZHOU YUXIN <zhou.yuxin@u.nus.edu>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:10:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Add acceptance tests for publish, cart, checkout and
 search

Sprint 2, WP5. 22 new tests, 35 in total.

The Sprint 1 retrospective agreed that the acceptance test for a story ships in
the same sprint as the story, so these cover every Sprint 2 rule that a
reviewer would otherwise have to take on trust:

- a cart spanning two sellers produces two orders, and the seller's own lines
  stay together in one of them
- the order line keeps its price after the seller raises the listing price
- checkout fails with 409 rather than overselling when the reservation cannot
  be taken, and the cart is left intact
- cancellation and expiry each release exactly what was reserved
- a buyer cannot order their own listing, and cannot touch another user's
  cart lines
- publishing strips script markup out of a description
- media keeps the order the seller arranged
- editing or delisting someone else's listing is refused, and delisting keeps
  the row
- highlighting treats the keyword as literal text, so a search for 'C++' does
  not blow up the regex

Sprint 1 noted that the suite mocks its collaborators and never starts the
Spring context, which is how two defects got through. That is still true here;
the Testcontainers work is scheduled for Sprint 3.
